title: Zentrum Presidential Candidate Selection 1932
subtitle: Choose our candidate for the 1932 presidential election.
view-if: player_party == 'z'
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: 1
max-visits: 1

@run_z_candidate
subtitle: This will cost us 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.z_campaign = 1;
Q.z_candidate_campaign = 1;
// Faction effects based on candidate
if (Q.z_candidate_1932 == "Marx") {
    Q.z_left_dissent -= 10;
    Q.z_center_dissent -= 10;
    Q.z_anti_fascist_dissent -= 5;
    Q.z_right_dissent += 5;
    Q.z_christian_unity_dissent += 5;
    Q.z_barons_dissent += 5;
    Q.workers_z += 2;
    Q.new_middle_z += 2;
    Q.catholics_z += 2;
} else if (Q.z_candidate_1932 == "Stegerwald") {
    Q.z_right_dissent -= 10;
    Q.z_christian_unity_dissent -= 5;
    Q.z_barons_dissent -= 5;
    Q.z_left_dissent += 10;
    Q.z_anti_fascist_dissent += 10;
    Q.z_center_dissent += 5;
    Q.catholics_z += 3;
    Q.rural_z += 3;
    Q.new_middle_z += 2;
    Q.old_middle_z += 2;
} else if (Q.z_candidate_1932 == "Kaas") {
    Q.z_christian_unity_dissent -= 10;
    Q.z_right_dissent -= 5;
    Q.z_barons_dissent -= 5;
    Q.z_left_dissent += 10;
    Q.z_anti_fascist_dissent += 5;
    Q.z_center_dissent += 5;
    Q.catholics_z += 4;
    Q.rural_z += 2;
}
Q.bvp_relations += 5;
Q.presidential_opinion += 5;
!}
max-visits: 1

We launch a presidential campaign with [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +] as our candidate. [? if z_candidate_1932 == "Marx": Wilhelm Marx's reputation as a moderate republican and former Chancellor gives us credibility across the democratic spectrum. The Left and Center factions are pleased, while the Right and Barons grumble about his "subservience to the Republic." ?][? if z_candidate_1932 == "Stegerwald": Adam Stegerwald's "leave the tower" strategy signals our openness to Protestant voters. The Right, Christian Unity, and Barons factions approve, but the Left and Anti-Fascist factions are deeply concerned about courting the nationalist right. ?][? if z_candidate_1932 == "Kaas": Ludwig Kaas represents Christian Unity above all. His candidacy prioritizes confessional solidarity, pleasing the Christian Unity, Right, and Barons factions, but alienating the Left and Anti-Fascist wings who fear a confessional ghetto. ?]

The BVP views our candidacy positively, seeing it as a defense of Catholic interests. [? if hindenburg_run: Hindenburg is privately annoyed—he had hoped the Zentrum would fall in line behind him. ?]

- @z_endorsements: Scout out potential endorsements for our candidate.
- @run_z_candidate: Reconsider our choice.

@z_endorsements
on-arrival: {!
// Reset support variables
Q.spd_support_z = 0;
Q.kpd_support_z = 0;
Q.ddp_support_z = 0;
Q.dvp_support_z = 0;
Q.lvp_support_z = 0;
Q.bvp_support_z = 0;
!}

We can't win this election alone. We need to build a coalition around [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +]. Who should we approach?

- @convince_spd_z: Convince the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> to back [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +].
- @convince_kpd_z: Convince the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> to back [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +].
- @convince_ddp_z: Convince the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to back [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +].
- @convince_lvp_z: Convince the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> to back [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +].
- @convince_dvp_z: Convince the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> to back [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +].
- @view_z_candidates: View party endorsements.
- @z_hope: We have concluded negotiations.

@z_hope
on-arrival: {!
// Check if liberal parties drop out
if ((Q.lvp_support_z && Q.lvp_formed || (Q.dvp_support_z || Q.ddp_support_z && (Q.liberal_reactionary_candidate_1932_name == "Gessler" || Q.liberal_vote - Q.ddp_votes < 8))) && Q.liberal_reactionary_candidate_1932) Q.lib_drop_out = 1;
// Check if center-right parties drop out
if (Q.bvp_support_z && Q.center_reactionary_candidate_1932) Q.z_drop_out = 1;

// Determine reactionary candidate changes based on dropouts
if ((Q.lib_drop_out && Q.z_drop_out || Q.z_drop_out && !Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 || Q.lib_drop_out && !Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932)) {
    Q.vorbeck_run = 1;
    Q.vorbeck_fallback = 1;
    Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 = "Lettow-Vorbeck";
    Q.reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = "Paul von Lettow-Vorbeck";
    Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
    Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
} else {
    if (Q.lib_drop_out) {
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Luther") {
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932;
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        } else if (Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Luther") {
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        }
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Gessler") {
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932;
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        } else if (Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Gessler") {
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        }
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Jarres") {
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932;
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        } else if (Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Jarres") {
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        }
    } else if (Q.z_drop_out) {
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Brüning") {
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932;
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        } else if (Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Brüning") {
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        }
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Adenauer") {
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932;
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        } else if (Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Adenauer") {
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        }
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Stegerwald") {
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932 = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932;
            Q.reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        } else if (Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 == "Stegerwald") {
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 = 0;
            Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932_disp = 0;
        }
    }
}
!}

Hopefully, the [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +] coalition is strong enough to rival [+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +][? if secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932: and [+ secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 +]?].

[? if lib_drop_out: Fortunately for us, [+ liberal_reactionary_candidate_1932_name +] has dropped out due to our courting of the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span>. ?][? if z_drop_out: Fortunately for us, [+ center_reactionary_candidate_1932_name +] has dropped out due to our courting of the BVP. ?]

[? if lib_drop_out and z_drop_out: However, the withdrawal of [+ liberal_reactionary_candidate_1932_name +] and [+ center_reactionary_candidate_1932_name +] has forced the entry of [+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +] into the race, serving as a candidate for the moderate right. ?][? if z_drop_out and not liberal_reactionary_candidate_1932: However, the withdrawal of [+ center_reactionary_candidate_1932_name +] has forced the entry of [+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +] into the race, serving as a candidate for the moderate right. ?][? if lib_drop_out and not center_reactionary_candidate_1932: However, the withdrawal of [+ liberal_reactionary_candidate_1932_name +] has forced the entry of [+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +] into the race, serving as a candidate for the moderate right. ?]

- @presidential_election_1932_round_1: The campaign begins.

@convince_spd_z
choose-if: z_votes >= spd_votes
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #c00000;">SPD</span> knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate.
max-visits: 1

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> is running [+ spd_candidate_1932_disp +] [? if spd_candidate_1932 == "Eckener": as a unity candidate ?]. [? if spd_relation >= 50: However, they might be convinced to drop their campaign and support [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +] instead. ?][? if spd_relation < 50: They do not seem willing to be convinced. ?]

- @spd_resources_z: Use our resources to persuade the SPD.
- @spd_relations_z: Use our good relations with the SPD.
- @z_endorsements: Forget about the SPD.

@spd_resources_z
view-if: spd_relation >= 60
choose-if: resources >= 2
subtitle: -2 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 2).
on-arrival: resources -= 2; spd_support_z = 1; z_relation += 5; kpd_relation -= 10; bvp_relations -= 5; presidential_opinion += 5; left_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent -= 5;
go-to: z_endorsements

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> agrees to endorse [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +]! This is a major breakthrough—a Catholic-Social Democrat presidential coalition. The KPD is furious, and the BVP is uneasy about the Left's influence.

@spd_relations_z
view-if: spd_relation >= 75
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations are not good enough.
on-arrival: spd_support_z = 1; z_relation += 5; kpd_relation -= 10; bvp_relations -= 5; presidential_opinion += 5; left_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent -= 5;
go-to: z_endorsements

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> agrees to endorse [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +]! This is a major breakthrough—a Catholic-Social Democrat presidential coalition. The KPD is furious, and the BVP is uneasy about the Left's influence.

@convince_kpd_z
choose-if: z_votes >= kpd_votes
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #700000;">KPD</span> knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate.
max-visits: 1

The <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> is supporting their own candidate, [+ communist_candidate_1932_disp +]. [? if kpd_relation >= 50: However, they might be convinced to drop their campaign and support [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +]. ?][? if kpd_relation < 50: They do not seem willing to be convinced. ?]

- @kpd_resources_z: Use our resources to persuade the KPD.
- @kpd_relations_z: Use our good relations with the KPD.
- @z_endorsements: Forget about the KPD.

@kpd_resources_z
view-if: kpd_relation >= 60 or (kpd_relation >= 45 and kpd_leader == "Conciliators")
choose-if: resources >= 3
subtitle: -3 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 3).
on-arrival: resources -= 3; kpd_support_z = 1; spd_relation -= 15; bvp_relations -= 15; z_relation -= 5; presidential_opinion -= 10; left_dissent -= 10; anti_fascist_dissent -= 10; right_dissent += 10; christian_unity_dissent += 10; barons_dissent += 10;
go-to: z_endorsements

The <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> now endorses [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +]! This shocks the political establishment—a Catholic-Communist alliance. The SPD feels betrayed, the BVP is horrified, and Hindenburg sees this as proof that the Zentrum has abandoned the Republic.

@kpd_relations_z
view-if: kpd_relation >= 75 or (kpd_leader == "Conciliators" and kpd_relation >= 55)
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations are not good enough.
on-arrival: kpd_support_z = 1; spd_relation -= 15; bvp_relations -= 15; z_relation -= 5; presidential_opinion -= 10; left_dissent -= 10; anti_fascist_dissent -= 10; right_dissent += 10; christian_unity_dissent += 10; barons_dissent += 10;
go-to: z_endorsements

The <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> now endorses [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +]! This shocks the political establishment—a Catholic-Communist alliance. The SPD feels betrayed, the BVP is horrified, and Hindenburg sees this as proof that the Zentrum has abandoned the Republic.

@convince_ddp_z
view-if: not lvp_formed
max-visits: 1
go-to: convince_ddp_success_z if (ddp_relation >= 50 and (ddp_ideology == "Right" or dstp_maintained)) or (ddp_relation >= 40 and ddp_ideology == "Moderate" and not dstp_maintained) or (ddp_relation >= 30 and ddp_ideology == "Left" and not dstp_maintained); convince_ddp_fail_z if not ((ddp_relation >= 50 and (ddp_ideology == "Right" or dstp_maintained)) or (ddp_relation >= 40 and ddp_ideology == "Moderate" and not dstp_maintained) or (ddp_relation >= 30 and ddp_ideology == "Left" and not dstp_maintained))

The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> vote has been falling over time, especially during the current economic depression, so they will probably be of minimal help. Still, every little bit counts. [? if z_candidate_1932 == "Marx": Marx's republican credentials make him palatable to the DDP's left wing. ?][? if z_candidate_1932 == "Stegerwald": Stegerwald's "leave the tower" strategy appeals to the DDP's right wing. ?][? if z_candidate_1932 == "Kaas": Kaas's confessional focus makes the DDP skeptical. ?]

@convince_ddp_success_z
on-arrival: ddp_support_z = 1; ddp_left += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 1; ddp_relation += 5
go-to: z_endorsements

Thanks to our friendly relations, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is now campaigning for [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +] in the election.

@convince_ddp_fail_z
on-arrival: ddp_support_z = 0; ddp_right += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 1; ddp_relation -= 5
go-to: z_endorsements

Unfortunately, under the influence of its business wing, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has refused to support a Zentrum candidate for the presidency.

@convince_lvp_z
view-if: lvp_formed
max-visits: 1
go-to: convince_lvp_success_z if ((lvp_relation >= 60 and lvp_ideology == "Right") or (lvp_relation >= 50 and lvp_ideology == "Moderate") or (lvp_relation >= 40 and lvp_ideology == "Left")) and lvp_leader != "Dingeldey"; convince_lvp_fail_z if not (((lvp_relation >= 60 and lvp_ideology == "Right") or (lvp_relation >= 50 and lvp_ideology == "Moderate") or (lvp_relation >= 40 and lvp_ideology == "Left")) and lvp_leader != "Dingeldey")

The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> vote has been falling over time, especially during the current economic depression, so they will probably be of minimal help to us. Still, every little bit counts. They will certainly be a hard party to convince, with vehemently anti-Catholic industrialists influencing the party. [? if z_candidate_1932 == "Stegerwald": Stegerwald's "leave the tower" strategy and Protestant outreach makes the LVP's right wing more receptive. ?][? if z_candidate_1932 != "Stegerwald": Our candidate's confessional profile makes the LVP deeply skeptical. ?]

@convince_lvp_success_z
on-arrival: lvp_support_z = 1; lvp_left += 3; lvp_relation += 5; new_middle_dnvp += new_middle_lvp*0.1 if not kvp_formed; old_middle_dnvp += old_middle_lvp*0.2 if not kvp_formed; rural_dnvp += rural_lvp*0.2 if not kvp_formed
go-to: z_endorsements

We have convinced the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> to give [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +] an official endorsement, to the shock of the party's industrial backers. In response, they begin to withdraw their support from the party en masse.

@convince_lvp_fail_z
on-arrival: lvp_support_z = 0; lvp_right += 3; lvp_relation -= 5
go-to: z_endorsements

Perhaps expectedly, we have failed to persuade the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> to back [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +], owing to their strong antipathy toward political Catholicism in general.

@convince_dvp_z
view-if: not lvp_formed and dvp_exist
max-visits: 1
go-to: convince_dvp_success_z if (dvp_relation >= 60 and dvp_ideology == "Right") or (dvp_relation >= 50 and dvp_ideology == "Moderate") or (dvp_relation >= 40 and dvp_ideology == "Left"); convince_dvp_fail_z if not ((dvp_relation >= 60 and dvp_ideology == "Right") or (dvp_relation >= 50 and dvp_ideology == "Moderate") or (dvp_relation >= 40 and dvp_ideology == "Left"))

The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> will be the most difficult of the bourgeois parties to convince, given their preference to keep their distance from political Catholicism. [? if z_candidate_1932 == "Stegerwald": Stegerwald's background as a Christian trade unionist and his "leave the tower" strategy presents a unique opportunity to win them over. ?][? if z_candidate_1932 != "Stegerwald": Our candidate's confessional profile makes the DVP deeply skeptical. ?]

@convince_dvp_success_z
on-arrival: dvp_support_z = 1; dvp_left += 3; dvp_relation += 5
go-to: z_endorsements

Thanks to our friendly relations, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> is now campaigning for [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +] in the election. However, they refuse to join Zentrum-led campaign committees and emphasize their independence from us.

@convince_dvp_fail_z
on-arrival: dvp_support_z = 0; dvp_right += 1; dvp_relation -= 3
go-to: z_endorsements

Unfortunately, under the influence of their industrialist wing, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> has rejected our overtures and will continue on their own path.

@view_z_candidates
go-to: z_endorsements

@support_hindenburg_z
view-if: hindenburg_run
on-arrival: {!
Q.z_support_reactionary = 1;
Q.z_choice = "Hindenburg";
Q.z_left_dissent += 15;
Q.z_anti_fascist_dissent += 15;
Q.z_center_dissent += 5;
Q.z_right_dissent -= 10;
Q.z_christian_unity_dissent -= 5;
Q.z_barons_dissent -= 10;
Q.workers_z -= 3;
Q.workers_nsdap += 3;
Q.unemployed_z -= 3;
Q.unemployed_nsdap += 3;
Q.catholics_z -= 2;
Q.catholics_kvp += 2;
Q.hindenburg_angry -= 30;
Q.bvp_relations -= 10;
if (Q.bvp_relations < 0) Q.bvp_relations = 0;
Q.presidential_opinion -= 10;
Q.spd_relation -= 5;
Q.kpd_relation -= 5;
!}

Despite his known <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> nature, Hindenburg has at least been keeping the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span> at bay. Thus, we must support him. [? if bruning_time: Hindenburg is reportedly dissatisfied with having been elected with the support of socialists and Catholics, blaming Brüning and his unpopular cabinet for this outcome. ?]

This decision deeply divides our party. The Left and Anti-Fascist factions are furious at supporting a man they see as the Republic's gravedigger. The Right, Christian Unity, and Barons factions are relieved. The BVP is alienated, viewing this as a betrayal of Catholic autonomy.

- @presidential_election_1932_round_1: The campaign begins.

@support_reactionary_z
view-if: not hindenburg_run and reactionary_candidate_1932 and reactionary_candidate_1932 != "Westarp" and reactionary_candidate_1932 != "Lettow-Vorbeck"
on-arrival: {!
Q.z_support_reactionary = 1;
Q.z_support_reactionary_1 = 1;
Q.z_choice = Q.reactionary_candidate_1932;
Q.z_left_dissent += 15;
Q.z_center_dissent += 10;
Q.z_anti_fascist_dissent += 10;
Q.z_right_dissent -= 5;
Q.z_christian_unity_dissent -= 5;
Q.z_barons_dissent -= 5;
Q.workers_z -= 3;
Q.workers_nsdap += 3;
Q.unemployed_z -= 3;
Q.unemployed_nsdap += 3;
Q.hindenburg_angry -= 30;
Q.bvp_relations -= 10;
if (Q.bvp_relations < 0) Q.bvp_relations = 0;
Q.presidential_opinion -= 10;
Q.kpd_nazi_urgency -= 1;
!}

For some reason, whether we are physically <i>unable</i> to run a candidate of our own, or genuinely believe that [+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +] is the safest bet for German democracy, we are supporting him now.

This decision divides our party. The Left, Center, and Anti-Fascist factions are unhappy about supporting a reactionary candidate. The Right, Christian Unity, and Barons are more supportive. The BVP is alienated.

- @presidential_election_1932_round_1: The campaign begins.

@support_reactionary_2_z
view-if: not hindenburg_run and secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 and secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 != "Westarp" and secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 != "Lettow-Vorbeck"
on-arrival: {!
Q.z_support_reactionary = 1;
Q.z_support_reactionary_2 = 1;
Q.z_choice = Q.secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932;
Q.z_left_dissent += 15;
Q.z_center_dissent += 10;
Q.z_anti_fascist_dissent += 10;
Q.z_right_dissent -= 5;
Q.z_christian_unity_dissent -= 5;
Q.z_barons_dissent -= 5;
Q.workers_z -= 3;
Q.workers_nsdap += 3;
Q.unemployed_z -= 3;
Q.unemployed_nsdap += 3;
Q.hindenburg_angry -= 30;
Q.bvp_relations -= 10;
if (Q.bvp_relations < 0) Q.bvp_relations = 0;
Q.presidential_opinion -= 10;
Q.kpd_nazi_urgency -= 1;
!}

For some reason, whether we are physically <i>unable</i> to run a candidate of our own, or genuinely believe that [+ secondary_reactionary_candidate_1932 +] is the safest bet for German democracy, we are supporting him now.

This decision divides our party. The Left, Center, and Anti-Fascist factions are unhappy about supporting a reactionary candidate. The Right, Christian Unity, and Barons are more supportive. The BVP is alienated.

- @presidential_election_1932_round_1: The campaign begins.

@support_spd_z
choose-if: not schleicher_spd
unavailable-subtitle: [? if schleicher_spd: As part of our deal with Schleicher, we are now obligated to support Hindenburg's re-election. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.z_support_spd = 1;
Q.z_left_dissent -= 10;
Q.z_anti_fascist_dissent -= 10;
Q.z_center_dissent -= 5;
Q.z_right_dissent += 10;
Q.z_christian_unity_dissent += 10;
Q.z_barons_dissent += 5;
Q.workers_z += 3;
Q.new_middle_z += 2;
Q.catholics_z -= 2;
Q.spd_relation += 10;
Q.kpd_relation -= 5;
Q.bvp_relations -= 15;
if (Q.bvp_relations < 0) Q.bvp_relations = 0;
Q.presidential_opinion += 10;
Q.hindenburg_angry += 20;
!}

We throw our support behind [+ spd_candidate_1932_disp +] of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>. This revives the spirit of the Weimar Coalition—Catholics and Social Democrats united for the Republic.

The Left and Anti-Fascist factions are pleased. The Right, Christian Unity, and Barons are deeply unhappy, seeing this as a betrayal of Catholic principles. The BVP is horrified and may split from us entirely. Hindenburg is furious at this "coalition of the Godless."

- @presidential_election_1932_round_1: The campaign begins.

@support_thalmann_z
choose-if: kpd_relation >= 50 and not schleicher_spd
unavailable-subtitle: [? if kpd_relation < 50 : We do not have good enough relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">Communists</span>, so they are not even willing to accept our support. ?][? if schleicher_spd: As part of our deal with Schleicher, we are now obligated to support Hindenburg's re-election. ?]

Supporting [+ communist_candidate_1932 +] is rather unpopular in our party, even if the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> accept our support. Are we sure?

- @support_thalmann_2_z: Yes, we will support <span style="color: #700000;">**[+ communist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>, despite the factional pleas against it.
- @run_z_candidate: Run [+ z_candidate_1932_disp +] instead.
- @support_hindenburg_z: Support <span style="color: #808080;">Hindenburg</span> instead.
- @support_spd_z: Support [+ spd_candidate_1932_disp +] instead.
- @abstain_z: Abstain from endorsing any candidate instead.

@support_thalmann_2_z
on-arrival: {!
Q.z_support_thalmann = 1;
Q.z_left_dissent -= 15;
Q.z_anti_fascist_dissent -= 15;
Q.z_center_dissent += 15;
Q.z_right_dissent += 20;
Q.z_christian_unity_dissent += 20;
Q.z_barons_dissent += 15;
Q.catholics_z -= 5;
Q.workers_z -= 3;
Q.workers_kpd += 5;
Q.kpd_relation += 15;
Q.spd_relation -= 15;
Q.bvp_relations -= 25;
if (Q.bvp_relations < 0) Q.bvp_relations = 0;
Q.presidential_opinion -= 20;
Q.hindenburg_angry += 40;
Q.kpd_nazi_urgency += 2;
!}

Fine. We have thrown our support to Chairman [+ communist_candidate_1932 +] of the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> to the dismay of our bourgeois allies and the BVP.

This is a catastrophic split. The Left and Anti-Fascist factions are the only ones pleased. The Center, Right, Christian Unity, and Barons are in open revolt. The BVP will almost certainly break away. Hindenburg views this as the final proof that the Zentrum has abandoned the Republic.

- @presidential_election_1932_round_1: The campaign begins.

@abstain_z
on-arrival: {!
Q.z_abstain_1932 = 1;
Q.z_left_dissent += 10;
Q.z_center_dissent += 10;
Q.z_right_dissent += 10;
Q.z_christian_unity_dissent += 10;
Q.z_anti_fascist_dissent += 10;
Q.z_barons_dissent += 10;
Q.workers_z -= 3;
Q.new_middle_z -= 2;
Q.old_middle_z -= 2;
Q.rural_z -= 2;
Q.catholics_z -= 2;

// campaign activities...
if (Q.nsdap_candidate_1932 == "Hitler") {
    Q.workers_nsdap += 2;
    Q.new_middle_nsdap += 4;
    Q.old_middle_nsdap += 4;
    Q.catholics_nsdap += 2;
    Q.rural_nsdap += 4;
    Q.unemployed_nsdap += 6;
    Q.new_middle_dnvp -= 3;
    Q.old_middle_dnvp -= 3;
    Q.rural_other -= 3;
    Q.catholics_other -= 3;
    Q.unemployed_kpd -= 3;
} else if (Q.nsdap_candidate_1932 == "Göring") {
    Q.old_middle_nsdap += 4;
    Q.old_middle_dnvp -= 4;
    Q.rural_nsdap += 2;
    Q.rural_dnvp -= 2;
    Q.workers_kpd += 3;
    Q.workers_nsdap -= 3;
}

if (Q.hindenburg_run) {
    if (Q.industrial_total_backing) {
        Q.hindenburg_funds += Q.industrial_ddp_backing;
        Q.hindenburg_funds += Q.industrial_lvp_backing;
        Q.hindenburg_funds += Q.industrial_dvp_backing;
        Q.hindenburg_funds += Q.industrial_dnvp_backing;
        Q.hindenburg_funds += ((100 - Q.nsdap_votes) / 25);
        if (Q.spd_in_government) Q.hindenburg_funds += ((100 - Q.kpd_votes) / 10);
    }
    if (Q.hindenburg_funds >= 5) {
        Q.new_middle_kvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 2;
        Q.old_middle_kvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 2;
        Q.rural_kvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 2;
        if (Q.dnvp_ideology == "Moderate") {
            Q.new_middle_dnvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 2;
            Q.old_middle_dnvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 2;
            Q.rural_dnvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 3;
        }
        Q.new_middle_other += Q.hindenburg_funds / 3;
        Q.old_middle_other += Q.hindenburg_funds / 3;
        Q.rural_other += Q.hindenburg_funds / 3;
        Q.new_middle_dvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 3;
        Q.old_middle_dvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 3;
        Q.rural_dvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 4;
        Q.new_middle_lvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 2;
        Q.old_middle_lvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 2;
        Q.rural_lvp += Q.hindenburg_funds / 4;
    }
    Q.hindenburg_unity = 10;
    if (Q.hindenburg_angry_bruning >= 75) Q.hindenburg_unity -= 1;
    if (Q.dvp_defect) Q.hindenburg_unity -= 1;
    if (Q.cnblp_defect) Q.hindenburg_unity -= 1;
    if (Q.second_bruning_cabinet_seen) Q.hindenburg_unity -= 1;
    if (Q.z_support_reactionary) Q.hindenburg_unity -= 3;
    if (Q.z_campaign || Q.z_support_thalmann || Q.kpd_support_z) Q.hindenburg_unity += 3;
    if (Q.hindenburg_unity >= 8) {
        Q.hindenburg_support += 2;
    }
    if (Q.hindenburg_unity >= 5) {
        Q.hindenburg_support += 2;
    }
    if (Q.hindenburg_unity >= 3) {
        Q.hindenburg_support += 1;
    }
    if (Q.hindenburg_unity) {
        Q.hindenburg_support += 1;
    }
    if (Q.hindenburg_support) {
        Q.new_middle_kvp += Q.hindenburg_support;
        Q.old_middle_kvp += Q.hindenburg_support;
        Q.rural_kvp += Q.hindenburg_support;
        if (Q.dnvp_ideology == "Moderate") {
            Q.new_middle_dnvp += Q.hindenburg_support;
            Q.old_middle_dnvp += Q.hindenburg_support;
            Q.rural_dnvp += Q.hindenburg_support;
        }
        Q.new_middle_ddp += Q.hindenburg_support / 3;
        Q.old_middle_ddp += Q.hindenburg_support / 3;
        Q.new_middle_other += Q.hindenburg_support / 1.5;
        Q.old_middle_other += Q.hindenburg_support / 1.5;
        Q.new_middle_dvp += Q.hindenburg_support / 3;
        Q.old_middle_dvp += Q.hindenburg_support / 3;
        Q.rural_other += Q.hindenburg_support / 1.5;
        Q.pro_republic += Q.hindenburg_support;
        if (!Q.kvp_formed) Q.rural_other += Q.hindenburg_support;
        Q.new_middle_nsdap -= Q.hindenburg_support;
        Q.old_nsdap -= Q.hindenburg_support;
        Q.rural_nsdap -= Q.hindenburg_support;
    }
    if (Q.rlb_nazi) {
        Q.rlb_hindenburg = 0;
        Q.rural_nsdap += Q.rural_other * 0.1;
        Q.rural_other *= 0.9;
        Q.rural_dnvp *= 0.9;
    } else if (!Q.rlb_nazi) {
        Q.rlb_hindenburg = 1;
        Q.rural_other += 4;
        if (Q.dnvp_ideology == "Moderate") {
            Q.rural_dnvp += 2;
        } else {
            Q.rural_kvp += 2;
        }
    }
}
!}

None of the candidates are worthy of our support, and we are either unable or unwilling to field a candidate of our own. This decision is widely seen as irresponsible, given our status as a major Catholic party. [? if hindenburg_run: Hindenburg is privately relieved by this, as receiving our endorsement would personally pain him. ?] The <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> will seize upon our lack of an endorsement, attempting to position [+ communist_candidate_1932_disp +] as the sole left-wing candidate in the race, likely drawing many of our voters as a protest vote.

This decision unites all six factions in their disapproval—each for different reasons. The Left and Anti-Fascist factions see it as surrender to the Right. The Right, Christian Unity, and Barons see it as a failure of leadership. The Center sees it as a betrayal of the party's duty to the Republic. The BVP is confused and alienated.

- @presidential_election_1932_round_1: The campaign begins.

